# Named-field constructor with @Child on [Map K V] type produces role "MapValues".
# This is the pattern used by TypeNode.Record in prelude.llt:
#   [Record@[as-type: [fn [let r] r]  guarding: true]
#     fields@Child: [Map String TypeNode]
#     open:         Bool]
#
# infer_child_role_from_type_expr detects [Map K T] → ChildRole::MapValues.
# The `field-annotations` key maps "fields" to {role: "MapValues"}.
# Non-@Child fields (open: Bool) do NOT appear in field-annotations.
[DictNode: [type [Record@[as-type: [fn [let r] r]  guarding: true]
  fields@Child: [Map String DictNode]
  open:         Bool]]]
[ann: [annotation-of Record]]
[has-field-anns: [has? "field-annotations" ann]]
[field-anns: [get "field-annotations" ann]]
[role: [get "role" [get "fields" field-anns]]]
[no-open: [not [has? "open" field-anns]]]
[result: [and has-field-anns [and [= role "MapValues"] no-open]]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Bool(true)})

=== warn
[TypeError] auto-indexed entries not supported in type expressions
[UndefinedVariable] undefined variable: Record
[UnificationFailure] cannot unify [] with <error>
